    "images_with_text_dpq4mA": {
      "type": "images-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_rnCkVY": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<em><strong>YOUR NECK AND YOUR HEAD ARE MORE CONNECTED THAN YOU THINK.&nbsp;</strong></em>",
            "heading_size": "title-md",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "full_text",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle",
            "highlighted_reveal": true
          }
        },
        "text_BbhqzP": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Long hours at a desk. Endless scrolling. Hours behind the wheel. Everyday habits can leave your neck feeling tight, stiff, and ready for a break.</p><p>Some headaches are linked to disorders of the neck, including the cervical spine and surrounding soft tissues.</p><p><strong>That’s why we start with the neck.</strong></p><p>Explore the research: <a href=\"https://ichd-3.org/11-headache-or-facial-pain-attributed-to-disorder-of-the-cranium-neck-eyes-ears-nose-sinuses-teeth-mouth-or-other-facial-or-cervical-structure/11-2-headache-attributed-to-disorder-of-the-neck/11-2-1-cervicogenic-headache/\">International Headache Society — ICHD-3</a></p>",
            "text_font": "heading",
            "text_size": "subtext-sm",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
